policies.pregnancyRecommendationFreeText:
Pregnancy:

According to the opinion of the Superior Council of Infectious Diseases of March 29, 2021:

Pregnancy is not a contraindication to vaccination against COVID-19;
Vaccination of pregnant women during phase 5b of the COVID-19 vaccine strategy is recommended due to their vulnerability to SARS-CoV-2 infection;
Vaccination of pregnant women should be prioritized when the benefits of vaccination outweigh the potential risks of vaccination:
In the event of comorbidity exposing the pregnant woman to a severe form of the disease (morbid obesity, chronic respiratory pathology, arterial hypertension, etc.);
In case of high risk of infection due to occupational exposure (health and care sector).
At this time, this recommendation applies only to mRNA-type vaccines, until more data are available for viral vector vaccines.

What are the contraindications for vaccination?
...
- pregnancy and the period of breastfeeding;

